From fe7c060be52411affa9a6a66b886935190f45edc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Levitte <levitte@openssl.foundation>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:41:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test_external_krb5: update krb5 submodule to 1.22.3

Update the krb5 submodule to krb5-1.22.3-final (f5bee90a).  The four
locally carried patches are present in 1.22.3 in equivalent form,
so they are dropped;  the release also carries the C23 strchr() fixes
that the gcc 15 default -std=gnu23 requires (the ubuntu-26.04 runners
fail the build with -Werror=discarded-qualifiers).

One small patch is carried instead:  the k5tls plugin lacks two
const qualifiers for OpenSSL 4.x APIs.

Resolves: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/issues/33794
Assisted-by: Pi:moonshotai/kimi-k3
Signed-off-by: Richard Levitte <levitte@openssl.foundation>
Reviewed-by: Dmitry Belyavskiy <beldmit@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Eugene Syromiatnikov <esyr@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Tue Nov 17 15:08:26 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33795
(cherry picked from commit 16796809d8f2fc92ce0bded75e6b60a9e1bba3bb)
